atus":"assembly-matched"},{"address":2300,"analyzer_agreement":{"analyzers":["IDA"],"reasons":[],"status":"agreed"},"artifacts":[{"kind":"comparison","path":"published/comparison-ida.json","sha256":"6213F1C3BA719B1F1B955C188CC47C6625E26ACC779C524E48F115208E3D1400"},{"kind":"consensus-reference","path":"published/consensus-reference.json","sha256":"BE0DDDB1BBA70FE5F19C0AA4A8990157AF7FC47FEE1E16116CBABF4B95C98EBB"}],"names":["+[VBE20DisplayDriverKernelServerInstance kernelServerInstance]"],"reason":"Build-generated; not ledgered against a source path. Raw bytes 2304 and 2305 differ (reference 00 00, rebuilt 58 24): the reference leaves _VBE20DisplayDriver_instance an unallocated common with a zero addend, while our kl_ld allocates it in __common. Both sides carry a length-2 relocation at that operand, so the masked extent compare in compare_vbe20.py is MATCH; binrecon's compare does not absorb it because the relocation target semantics differ (undefined common against a defined address). Exempt at ledger level, but flagged: the cause is unidentified and it may matter at load time. Task 9's boot gate is what would reveal that, and it is blocked on a separate kernel spec, so a load failure there must not be misdiagnosed. See reconstruction/divergences.md.","reviewer":"Pat Raynor","size":12,"source_line":null,"source_path":null,"status":"control-flow-confirmed"},{"address":2312,"analyzer_agreement":{"analyzers":["IDA"],"reasons":[],"status":"agreed"},"artifacts":[{"kind":"comparison","path":"published/comparison-ida.json","sha256":"6213F1C3BA719B1F1B955C188CC47C6625E26ACC779C524E48F115208E3D1400"},{"kind":"consensus-reference","path":"published/consensus-reference.json","sha256":"BE0DDDB1BBA70FE5F19C0AA4A8990157AF7FC47FEE1E16116CBABF4B95C98EBB"}],"names":["+[VBE20DisplayDriverVersion driverKitVersionForVBE20DisplayDriver]"],"reason":"Build-generated; not ledgered against a source path. Raw byte 2316 differs (reference a4, rebuilt f4): +driverKitVersionForVBE20DisplayDriv